1. Download the Q5_GitMergeConflict folder from ma'am's Drive (Download all), extract it to the
Desktop and open it in VS Code (File > Open Folder).
2. In Drive, conflict-demo is a Google Doc - open it, copy the text and save it in VS Code as
conflict-demo.txt. Then delete the downloaded .docx copies from the folder.
3. Run in terminal:
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"
git branch -M main
git branch feature
git branch
SCREENSHOT 1: VS Code terminal - init + commit output
SCREENSHOT 2: VS Code terminal - git branch output (main and feature)
4. Run in terminal:
git checkout feature
5. In conflict-demo.txt change the Venue line to Venue: Open Air Theatre and save.
6. Run in terminal:
git commit -am "Feature branch: change venue"
git checkout main
7. In conflict-demo.txt (now back on main) change the Venue line to Venue: Seminar Hall 3 and
save.
8. Run in terminal:
git commit -am "Main branch: change venue"
git log --oneline --graph --all
git merge feature
SCREENSHOT 3: VS Code terminal - git log --graph showing two branches
SCREENSHOT 4: VS Code terminal - red "CONFLICT" message
9. Terminal shows CONFLICT. Open conflict-demo.txt - you will see the conflict markers:
<<<<<<< HEAD
Venue: Seminar Hall 3
=======
Venue: Open Air Theatre
>>>>>>> feature
SCREENSHOT 5: VS Code editor - conflict-demo.txt showing <<<<<<< ======= >>>>>>>
10. Delete the 3 marker lines and keep only one Venue line (e.g. Venue: Seminar Hall 3). Save.
(Or click Accept Current Change in VS Code.)
